  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>From La Favière beach, this coastal path runs along the coast towards the Esquillette point, then on to Cap Blanc, with views of Île du Levant, Port-Cros and the Corniche des Maures. The town of Bormes-les-Mimosas describes this "Plage de la Favière – Cap Blanc" section as a 7 km path in a listed site.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The tourist office gives 4 km (3 h) to reach the Esquillette point; beyond that, the path to Cap Blanc is considered difficult and passes near the Domaine de Bénat, a private estate. There is no path between Cap Blanc and Cabasson beach. Dogs are accepted on hikes, on a leash (tourist office FAQ), which matters all the more near the cliffs.</p>
      <p>Direction (tourist office): facing the sea on La Favière beach, turn right; the path follows the coast and its coves to Cap Blanc, at the far south of the commune, where you must turn back (the section beyond is under study and restoration; about 4 h round trip, little elevation). The section that would link this path to the Cabasson one is closed to the public by municipal order for safety reasons (town).</p>
      <p>The hike may be closed when fire risk is high on the Corniche des Maures: check risque-prevention-incendie.fr/var before setting off. The La Favière car park (more than 550 spaces) is paid from 15 June to 15 September, 8am to 7pm (€8 per day), and free the rest of the year.</p>
      <p>Beach: from 15 June to 30 September, the town allows leashed dogs only on part of Cabasson beach (near the fort, east side of the groyne) and on Gouron beach; La Favière beach is not on that list in summer. The town's parks are closed to dogs (tourist office FAQ).</p>
      <h3>Worth checking before you go</h3>
      <p>The car park rates are those on the town's page; the tourist office, for its part, announces car parks at €11-13 (undated page). The state of the path after the annual works and any closure for fire risk should be checked the day before.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: check the fire risk level before setting off and keep your dog on a leash near the cliffs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Bormes-les-Mimosas and its La Favière harbour are right next door, a great base to extend the day.</p>
    </div>

